WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.476 --> 00:00:16.584
My name is Seti, and I am a scribe living in Egypt in the year 1353 BC.

2
00:00:17.324 --> 00:00:22.667
A scribe is someone who reads and writes for people who cannot, and because not many people are

3
00:00:22.748 --> 00:00:24.809
literate, scribes are very valuable.

4
00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:29.952
We help government officials run the country and businessmen keep track of their goods.

5
00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:36.486
Scribes write down histories of great battles, the number of cattle in a herd, and anything else that

6
00:00:36.526 --> 00:00:37.447
needs to be remembered.

7
00:00:38.647 --> 00:00:42.809
To become a scribe, young boys usually have to be born into the profession.

8
00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:48.951
My father was a scribe, so I became one too, and at seven years old, I went to

9
00:00:48.991 --> 00:00:49.772
a palace school.

10
00:00:50.992 --> 00:00:57.375
Students sat around the teacher and sang songs to memorize different words, and after we learned the words,

11
00:00:57.835 --> 00:01:00.456
we would practice writing on pieces of broken pottery.

12
00:01:01.404 --> 00:01:04.925
If a student made a mistake, the teacher would hit him on the back with a stick and

13
00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:09.586
say, "A boy's ears are in his back—he will listen only when he is beaten!"

14
00:01:10.446 --> 00:01:15.848
Student scribes always made sure they knew their lessons well, if only to avoid the teacher's anger.

15
00:01:16.908 --> 00:01:21.129
It took me four years to learn how to read and write, and I learned to write in

16
00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:24.450
two different ways: hieroglyphic and hieratic.

17
00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:29.812
A hieroglyph is a picture that tells a reader what a word means, and each picture is a

18
00:01:29.872 --> 00:01:32.273
word or sound in the Egyptian language.

19
00:01:33.453 --> 00:01:37.896
A scribe must memorize and be able to write over seven hundred different pictures.

20
00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:44.660
Hieroglyphs are sacred, which means they are special to the gods, so they are used for tombs and

21
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:53.865
monuments. For everyday communication, such as business letters, receipts, and government documents, we use hieratic writing, an alphabet

22
00:01:53.885 --> 00:01:56.266
of simple letters that are based on the hieroglyphs.

23
00:01:57.907 --> 00:02:02.737
After four years of school, I became an apprentice on the estate of a wealthy man who employed

24
00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:04.538
several scribes to keep his accounts.

25
00:02:05.499 --> 00:02:10.501
They taught me how to write his official letters and keep records of his possessions and trading activities.

26
00:02:11.561 --> 00:02:17.383
For example, I learned to write down the day, month, and season of each trade, what items were

27
00:02:17.424 --> 00:02:21.145
traded and received, and the name of the merchant involved in the transaction.

28
00:02:21.985 --> 00:02:26.347
I also had to carefully note the measure of what was traded whether it was a basket of

29
00:02:26.387 --> 00:02:31.071
grain, a jar of oil, a tall slave, or a large cow's head.

30
00:02:32.212 --> 00:02:36.496
Even though I wasn't paid, I gained a lot of experience working on a large estate.

31
00:02:37.737 --> 00:02:43.882
After my five-year apprenticeship, I was hired by the great pharaoh Amenhotep III as a scribe for the

32
00:02:43.943 --> 00:02:44.623
royal family.

33
00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:50.769
Amenhotep III has ruled Egypt for 37 years and has made our country very wealthy.

34
00:02:51.409 --> 00:02:56.561
He has ordered many statues and temples to be built, so scribes are needed to organize all the

35
00:02:56.621 --> 00:03:00.222
work and record all the supplies needed and used for the construction.

36
00:03:01.022 --> 00:03:07.564
In my position I write all the pharaoh's official letters to foreign kings in distant lands, and letters

37
00:03:07.604 --> 00:03:11.965
for royal family members who wish to keep in touch with relatives throughout the country.

38
00:03:12.885 --> 00:03:17.967
Every year scribes also write down how much grain has been grown and then calculate how long the

39
00:03:18.007 --> 00:03:20.327
grain will last after it is stored in the grain house.

40
00:03:21.308 --> 00:03:27.482
Storing grain can be difficult as fire, rats, and insects can be a problem, so the scribes must

41
00:03:27.522 --> 00:03:30.303
keep a careful tally of the grain as it sits in the grain house.

42
00:03:31.324 --> 00:03:39.067
In addition to recording agricultural matters, scribes read, copy, and archive all government documents, tax records, and the

43
00:03:39.108 --> 00:03:43.269
religious laws of the country each year to make sure the libraries are up-to-date.

44
00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:48.612
More than anyone else, scribes are very well-informed about the business of Egypt.

45
00:03:49.488 --> 00:03:53.692
Scribes are also hired to write magic prayers and the names of the deceased on their coffins.

46
00:03:54.573 --> 00:04:01.298
Egyptians believe that when a person dies, he or she lives on in an afterlife, so scribes write

47
00:04:01.378 --> 00:04:06.122
magical words to protect the spirits of the dead and to help the person find a path to

48
00:04:06.142 --> 00:04:06.703
the afterlife.

49
00:04:07.904 --> 00:04:13.969
These magical prayers have always been written in the pyramids for the pharaohs, but long ago scribes started

50
00:04:14.009 --> 00:04:16.011
writing coffin prayers for common people too.

51
00:04:16.671 --> 00:04:21.891
When I write, I use paper called papyrus, which is made from the stem of a reed that

52
00:04:21.931 --> 00:04:23.292
grows along the Nile River.

53
00:04:24.153 --> 00:04:28.777
The stem strips are cut, moistened, and layered on top of each other at right angles.

54
00:04:29.497 --> 00:04:32.920
Then they are pounded together and dried to make a sheet of paper.

55
00:04:33.641 --> 00:04:39.025
If I must write a long report, I paste the pages together to form a scroll that's rolled

56
00:04:39.125 --> 00:04:40.306
on two wooden handles.

57
00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:47.051
Sometimes I write on pottery, stone tablets, or parchment, which is made of animal hides stretched thin and

58
00:04:47.091 --> 00:04:53.378
dried. I have a wooden tablet called a palette with two holders for red and black ink, which

59
00:04:53.438 --> 00:04:56.559
is made with papyrus juice and another material for color.

60
00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.061
Red ink is made from red clay, and black ink is made from soot.

61
00:05:02.322 --> 00:05:07.244
The palette also holds my writing brush, which is made from the hollow stem of a grasslike plant

62
00:05:07.284 --> 00:05:07.904
called a rush.

63
00:05:08.704 --> 00:05:12.686
Before I can write with my brush, I chew on the end to soften it, so it can

64
00:05:12.726 --> 00:05:13.566
absorb the ink.

65
00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:17.728
The hieroglyph that stands for "scribe" is a picture of the equipment I use.

66
00:05:18.688 --> 00:05:24.552
Because of our ability to read and write, most people think scribes have mysterious powers from the gods,

67
00:05:25.452 --> 00:05:27.553
so we are treated well and get very rich.

68
00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:33.937
Because I'm a royal scribe, no one gives me orders except the pharaoh; therefore I don't have to

69
00:05:33.977 --> 00:05:34.778
do any hard work.

70
00:05:35.558 --> 00:05:39.941
The ability to read and write has given me a good life, but I feel sorry for the

71
00:05:40.001 --> 00:05:41.202
ordinary workers in the kingdom.

72
00:05:41.922 --> 00:05:44.964
Tired bodies and low pay are their only reward.
